;; Campaign play only (0.4.31): 8-1's coin room is Jason's on-foot dungeon seen from the side
;; (`bm-vault`, the underground still): the overhead dungeon's steel plates, grilles and riveted
;; blocks before a wall of panels and a vent grille, to the dungeon's tune. Elsewhere (level
;; select, ?level=8-1) it looks as it always did.
;;
;; Campaign only (0.4.54, docs/STORY.md "Sophia III's way in"): the real way down to Sophia III's
;; garage. The 10-coin brick (12,9) is a key box: bumped from the floor below (three tiles up, a
;; plain jump for every hero) the key drops out of its underside to the floor. Carried to the
;; locked blast door (4, rows 11-12) it opens the door by itself; UP goes down into the garage.
;; Jason, who lost the key, stands between. Once Sophia III is freed the door stands open and the
;; brick keeps its coins. Elsewhere the room is as it always was.
